1b:["$","figure","1",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-left border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50","children":[["$","th","0",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Level"}],["$","th","1",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Broadly performs"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Emergency Medical Responder (EMR)"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Immediate lifesaving care with minimal equipment"}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Emergency Medical Technician (EMT)"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Basic life support, assessment, oxygen, and a limited set of medications"}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Advanced EMT (AEMT)"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"EMT scope plus IV access and additional medications"}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Paramedic"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Advanced life support — cardiac monitoring, intubation, a wide drug formulary"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"EMS certification levels"}]]}]
1c:["$","p","2",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"EMTs work under medical direction. A physician medical director authorizes what the service's EMTs may do, expressed as protocols. Some actions are standing orders you carry out without contacting anyone; others require online medical control, meaning you contact a physician before acting. Your scope is the intersection of your certification level, your state, and your service's protocols — and it is not identical anywhere."}]
1d:["$","figure","3",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-left border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50","children":[["$","th","0",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Step"}],["$","th","1",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"What it involves"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"State-approved EMT course"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Classroom, skills lab, and clinical or field time — commonly 150 to 200 hours"}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Course completion"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Including a psychomotor skills evaluation"}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Cognitive (written) exam"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Computer-based. Most states use the NREMT exam, which is computer-adaptive: 70 to 120 questions in up to 2 hours. Confirm which exam your state uses"}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Psychomotor (skills) exam"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Hands-on skill stations, in the form your state requires"}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"State licensure or certification"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"The state grants the credential; NREMT is a common prerequisite"}]]}],["$","tr","5",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Recertification"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Continuing education on a defined cycle. National Registry certification renews every 2 years, with 40 continuing education credits or by retaking the exam"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"The certification pathway"}]]}]
1e:["$","div","4",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-blue-50 border-blue-400","children":[false,"In New York State, the Department of Health's Bureau of EMS certifies EMTs. After a NYS-approved course, you need a skills evaluation the Bureau accepts, then one of two approved cognitive exams: the New York State exam, scheduled through the state's testing vendor (PSI) at a test center or, for EMTs, by live remote proctoring, or the National Registry cognitive exam. You have three attempts, within two years of your course end date. New York EMT certifications issued after July 1, 2024 last 48 months."]}]
1f:["$","div","5",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-yellow-50 border-yellow-400","children":[false,"There is no route to EMT certification that skips the hands-on component. Airway management, spinal motion restriction, splinting, lifting, and moving a patient are psychomotor skills assessed by demonstration, and no online course can teach or verify them. Any provider claiming to certify you as an EMT entirely online is not offering something recognized."]}]
20:["$","div","6",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-blue-50 border-blue-400","children":[false,"Two things worth knowing before you enroll. The work is physically demanding — lifting and carrying patients is routine, and back injuries are a serious occupational risk that can end a career. And the psychological load is real: you will attend calls involving children, violence, and death. Services increasingly provide critical incident support, and using it is a professional norm rather than a weakness."]}]
21:["$","$L25","7",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"Can you become a certified EMT through an online-only course?","options":["Yes, if the provider is accredited","No — certification requires a state-approved course with hands-on skills and clinical or field hours, plus a psychomotor evaluation","Yes, provided you pass the NREMT cognitive exam","Only for the EMR level"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"The psychomotor component cannot be delivered or assessed online. State-approved courses may deliver didactic content online, but the skills lab, the clinical or field hours, and the practical evaluation are in person. Passing the cognitive exam alone does not certify anyone.","optionRationales":["Accreditation does not remove the hands-on requirement; approved programs still include it.","Correct — the practical component is mandatory and in person.","The cognitive exam is one part. Skills evaluation and course completion are separate requirements.","EMR also requires hands-on skills training."]}}]
22:["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-12","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-[40px] sm:leading-[1.05]","children":"Challenge"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft","children":"Apply what you've learned in this lesson."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-md border border-gray-200 p-8","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Research the specific pathway where you live before committing."}],["$","ol","1",{"start":"$undefined","className":"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 marker:font-semibold marker:text-primary-600","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Find your state EMS office and list the requirements for EMT certification: course hours, exams, and any background check."}],["$","li","1",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Find two state-approved EMT programs near you. Record cost, length, schedule, and whether clinical placements are arranged for you."}],["$","li","2",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Find out which certification exams your state uses, then look up that exam's current format and the recertification cycle."}],["$","li","3",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Write down honestly what in the role concerns you most, and find out what support services in your area provide for it."}]]}]]}]}]]}]
